> Installing Applications

### Installing with Shelly

step 1: open Shelly
from the runner (*SUPER+SPACE*), *SUPER+Y*, or the button in the top bar.

step 2: set up Shelly (first launch only)
pick which repositories to use. pacman + AUR recommended, flatpak optional.

step 3: select repository
tabs for pacman, AUR, and flatpak. use in this order.

prefer pacman for all software unless it isn't available there.
use AUR if pacman doesn't have it. -git versions build from source, -bin versions are prebuilt.
flatpak is the last option. use flatseal to manage permissions.

### Installing with Unipkg TUI

press *super+shift+Y* or run `unipkg launch-tui`

select install, then your package manager of choice.
searchable list with package info. multi-select with *tab*, enter to install.

also works from CLI: `unipkg install any <packagename>`
this tries all package managers in the order listed in ~/.config/unipkg/unipkg.conf

### Installing with Pacman Directly

`sudo pacman -S <package>`

### Installing from the AUR

SNAPS-OS comes with yay as its AUR helper.

`yay -S <packagename>`

### Best Practice

1. check pacman first (most stable, well-integrated)
2. if not found, check AUR (more software, less moderated)
3. if neither works, use flatpak (sandboxed, cross-platform)
